278	// BOOTSTRAP ONLY, and gated like the badge row for the same reason: this is a one-time
279	// seed of a file the repo then OWNS. A nightly that re-created it would resurrect a
280	// pack the owner deliberately deleted, and a nightly that rewrote it would overwrite
281	// the rules it exists to hold.
